cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Vox in your research or build on its design, please cite it."
type: software
title: "Vox: The AI-Native Programming Language"
abstract: >
  Vox is a pre-1.0 AI-native, full-stack programming language that compiles to Rust
  (backend) and TypeScript (frontend). The compiler enforces a null-free type system
  (absence is Option[T], failure is Result[T, E]) to shrink the hallucination surface
  for generated code. MCP tools, interpreted durable workflows (journal replay), and
  actor-based concurrency are first-class language constructs. Generated Rust workflows
  are not yet full durable state machines.
authors:
  - family-names: "Brainerd"
    given-names: "Bert"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vox-foundation/vox"
url: "https://voxlang.org"
license: Apache-2.0
